    "summaryAr": "Location: UK, central Europe, and Latin America Remote | Full-time Compensation: Competitive Compensation Our client is seeking an experienced, full-time Product Designer to shape the core user experience of their trend intelligence platform. In this role, the designer will play a key part in designing and evolving the platform’s primary dashboard—where brand innovation teams, product marketers, social media teams, a",
    "descriptionAr": "Location: UK, central Europe, and Latin America Remote | Full-time Compensation: Competitive Compensation Our client is seeking an experienced, full-time Product Designer to shape the core user experience of their trend intelligence platform. In this role, the designer will play a key part in designing and evolving the platform’s primary dashboard—where brand innovation teams, product marketers, social media teams, and agencies explore trends, generate reports, and interact with LLM-powered features. As the platform rebuilds around LLM-driven capabilities, the successful candidate will be responsible for defining not just how features look, but how complex data and AI experiences should function. The primary focus is transforming dense, aggregated trend data into clear, intuitive, and actionable insights. This position joins a close-knit Frontend & UX team reporting directly to the Frontend Lead. The role is 100% remote and open to candidates based between US Central Time (UTC−6) and Central European Time (UTC+1). Candidates must be available during core collaboration hours of 9:00 AM–12:00 PM Eastern Standard Time (2:00 PM–5:00 PM UK / 3:00 PM–6:00 PM CET). Key Responsibilities End-to-End Product Design: Own features from initial framing to final launch, partnering closely with engineering leadership to deliver written proposals, user flows, prototypes, and Figma specifications. Problem Identification & Solution Design: Independently identify user pain points through customer calls, interviews, user feedback, and usage data to build compelling product proposals. AI & LLM Experience Design: Define user interactions for AI features (chat, automated reports, inline summaries), establish standards for insight attribution and uncertainty handling, and help refine the voice and structure of AI-generated content. Design System Management: Own the principles and Figma library for the design system, partnering with frontend engineers to align with the React component library and establish robust data visualization and AI UX patterns. UX Quality & Feedback Loops: Co-own product metrics, user feedback tracking, and quality evaluation rubrics for LLM outputs alongside the Frontend Lead. Note: This position focuses strictly on product/UI/UX design. It does not involve writing production code, managing brand/marketing assets, or overseeing back-end API integrations. Requirements Qualifications Experience: 3+ years of product design experience, ideally owning features end-to-end within a B2B or SaaS platform. Product Thinking: Strong strategic perspective with a proven ability to define what to build and why , backed by a portfolio demonstrating strong problem-framing abilities. Domain Focus: Experience designing data-heavy products, such as dashboards, analytics platforms, or reporting tools. Design Systems: Proven track record of working within and contributing to scalable design component libraries. Tools & AI Integration: High proficiency in Figma, with active integration of AI tools into day-to-day design workflows and a strong curiosity regarding LLM product experiences. Communication: Excellent written English skills, capable of producing clear proposals and documentation in an asynchronous remote environment. Schedule: Location within UTC−6 to UTC+1, with full availability during core collaboration hours (9:00 AM–12:00 PM EST). Preferred Qualifications (Nice to Have) Experience as the founding or primary designer on a product team. Hands-on experience building or evolving design systems adopted by engineering teams. Direct experience designing AI features or creating evaluation rubrics for LLM output quality. Expertise in advanced data visualization patterns. Familiarity with consumer goods, beauty, food & beverage, or marketing intelligence platforms. Capability to build rapid functional prototypes using AI-assisted tools to evaluate live outputs. Benefits Competitive compensation package tailored to experience. Collaborative, high-impact environment with direct influence on core product direction. Opportunity to work closely alongside senior design leadership. Flexible starting timeline (target start date in January, with early onboarding available). Interview Process Initial Video Screening: A brief introductory video conversation to discuss background, expectations, and role fit. Personality Assessment: An online assessment to evaluate working style and team dynamics. Design Leadership Interview: A 30-minute introductory chat with the Lead Designer. Screen-Recorded Case Study: A flexible, practical exercise (details currently being finalized) to demonstrate hands-on design methodology and execution. Final Interview: A concluding conversation with key stakeholders to review results and align on next steps. Due to the high volume of applications we anticipate, we regret that we are unable to provide individual feedback to all candidates. If you do not hear back from us within 4 weeks of your application, please assume that you have not been successful on this occasion. We genuinely appreciate your interest and wish you the best in your job search. Commitment to Equality and Accessibility: At MLabs, we are committed to offer equal opportunities to all candidates. We ensure no discrimination, accessible job adverts, and providing information in accessible formats. Our goal is to foster a diverse, inclusive workplace with equal opportunities for all. If you need any reasonable adjustments during any part of the hiring process or you would like to see the job-advert in an accessible format please let us know at the earliest opportunity by emailing ----- Ltd collects and processes the personal information you provide such as your contact details, work history, resume, and other relevant data for recruitment purposes only. This information is managed securely in accordance with MLabs Ltd’s Privacy Policy and Information Security Policy, and in compliance with applicable data protection laws. Your ",
